 "description": "The overnight fit continued with slow speed noise (description, discarded seeds).\n\nThe overnight fit's answer misses the wild type on two statistics: the roaming speed's 10-s window\n90th percentile and the small lawn's roaming-bout length (`overnight_grade.json`). Slow speed noise\nat 3 s fixes both on that answer, but shifts the roaming speed's median up and the on-lawn onset\nrate down (`speednoise.json`), as an answer tuned without it would. Here the fit continues with the\nnoise on and its timescale fitted:\n\n- the model, bounds and objective: `overnight.py`'s (the six families plus the three mutants at half\n  the objective, both guards), on `speednoise.py`'s model (the timescale appended as the last entry,\n  on [0, 1] in its log units over 0.25-300 s);\n- the start: the overnight answer with the timescale at 3 s;\n- the search: sep-CMA at population 48, sigma0 0.03, 200 animals a candidate, 50 generations on 16\n  workers, saved every generation and resumable.\n\nReadouts every 10 generations on 200 animals (786,000,000 + i). The stop rule, fixed before the run:\nat generation 30, stop if the readout D is more than 0.5 above its generation-0 readout. The\nverdict, fixed before the run: the final answer graded with presence on 5 populations\n(790,000,000 + 200\u00b7g + i) passes if the wild type passes in at least 3 of 5, and tph-1 and tax-4\neach pass in at least 3 of 5.\n\nSeeds: fit animals 785,000,000 + 200\u00b7k + i; CMA 9488. Run from the repository root.\n",
